{
  "info": {
    "name": "authservice - Seed test accounts",
    "description": "Run this folder in the Collection Runner (or `postman collection run <file> -i \"Seed test accounts (one-click)\"`)\nto create and approve one account per role. Every account uses the password in `{{seedPassword}}`.\n\n| Role | Email | clientId |\n|---|---|---|\n| SUPER_ADMIN | superadmin@uyir.test | superadmin-portal |\n| ADMIN | admin@uyir.test | admin-portal |\n| PATIENT | patient@uyir.test | patient-app |\n| DOCTOR | doctor@uyir.test | service-provider-app |\n| HOSPITAL | hospital@uyir.test | service-provider-app |\n| LS | ls@uyir.test | service-provider-app |\n| AMBULANCE_DRIVER | ambulance-driver@uyir.test | service-provider-app |\n| PRO | pro@uyir.test | service-provider-app |\n| LSC | lsc@uyir.test | service-provider-app |\n| ECG | ecg@uyir.test | service-provider-app |\n| HP | hp@uyir.test | service-provider-app |\n| HBC | hbc@uyir.test | service-provider-app |\n\nSafe to re-run: existing accounts return 409 (counted as OK) and only PENDING `@uyir.test` accounts get approved.\nApproving is done by the Super Admin, so nobody else's pending account is touched.\n\nThe run makes 13 calls to the auth rate limiter (12 registers + 1 login). The default limit is\n20 per 15 minutes per IP, so a second run straight after the first will get 429s - wait, or\nstart the server with a higher `AUTH_RATE_LIMIT_MAX`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:4000"
    },
    {
      "key": "seedPassword",
      "value": "Uyir@12345"
    },
    {
      "key": "seedSuperAdminToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "seedPendingIds",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "seedApproveId",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Register Super Admin",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// 201 = created now, 409 = already exists from an earlier run. Both are fine.",
              "pm.test(\"account exists (201 created or 409 already registered)\", () => {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([201, 409]);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"superadmin@uyir.test\",\n  \"password\": \"{{seedPassword}}\",\n  \"clientId\": \"superadmin-portal\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/email/register",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "auth",
            "email",
            "register"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
